{"slug": "k1110-golf-cart-audio-system", "status": "skip", "reason": "No single store can hold 2 or more items that honestly make a golf cart audio system, with each item sourced today (2026-11-10). (1) Amazon is the only store that could hold both a soundbar and a 48V-to-12V reducer, but amzcheck.py and WebFetch were blocked (blocked:true / HTTP 503) for the BOSS BRT26RGB (B08GXYJS1B), the Roykaw reducer (B086C32FK1) and the 9.99WORLD MALL reducer (B07449LX7K). The only reducer that loaded was a second 9.99WORLD MALL reducer, B0GS7XL6LT ('Universal Golf Cart Voltage Reducer DC Converter 36V or 48V to 12V 30 A 360W'). Its title gives no input range, so it can't be shown to tolerate the 58.4 V charge voltage of a 48V lithium pack that cartvoltage.com and the K2/K5 reports use as the test. The Cellena listing (B07D5QVPWK) gives 30–56 V input, which fails that test. Searches turned up no Amazon listing for either reducer whose 60 V-plus ceiling is sourced: Victron Orion-Tr 48/12-20A (32–70 V) and Hornet Energy HN-VRD-12V-30A (36–60 V). (2) Vatrer (awin:vatrer) sells the 48V/72V-to-12V 25 A reducer and a 48V battery kit but no speaker or soundbar, so its cart has no audio. (3) Fugoo (awin:fugoo) sells the Tough 2.0 2-Pack at $99.99 as one bundle SKU, but searches for 'mount' and 'strap' (and K4's) found no mount or other fitting item. That makes one item, not a 2-item kit, and a no-wiring speaker pair doesn't match any of the K1–K3 angles, which are all about wiring a reducer. (4) Redodo (awin:redodo) sells only the 48V battery conversion kit. The strongest angle, K3 (standout 2: on a lithium kit with a shunt monitor, such as Redodo's 500 A shunt, the reducer's negative must land on the shunt's load side or the monitor never counts the stereo's draw), is sourced and could carry the page. To proceed, it needs a verified Amazon reducer listing with a stated input ceiling above 58.4 V, plus the BOSS BRT26RGB re-checked once Amazon stops blocking amzcheck."}
